  "docTitle": "Hotel Booking - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design hotel booking (Zepto, Expedia, Wayfair): per-night inventory counts, holds that expire, a booking state machine, pricing decorators, cancellation policies and a per-hotel lock, plus the SQL version, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 70 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 120 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine-coding case study</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 30 of 45</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Hotel Booking</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Rooms are sold by the night, not by the seat. We start from a hotel receptionist's paper calendar and build a design with room inventory by date, 15-minute holds that expire, stackable pricing rules, per-hotel cancellation policies and a booking state machine, then code it in Java, Python and C++ and prove that eight guests racing for the last room produce exactly one winner.</p>\n"
  },
